Research attribution
--------------------

The documentation cites prior work on POMDPs, active perception, value of
information, Subjective Logic, Evidential Deep Learning, CNABU,
uncertainty-informed manipulation and vision-language-action models. Full
bibliographic entries are in references.bib.

No source code, pretrained model, mesh, image, dataset or other asset from the
following projects is included in this repository:

* NilsDengler/manipulation_enhanced_map_prediction (CNABU supplementary code)
* NilsDengler/view-point-pushing
* Joringell/ASA (Act-Sense-Act / CoMe-VLA)
* openvla/openvla or moojink/openvla-oft
* octo-models/octo
* google-research/saycan

At the audit date (2026-08-04), the root repositories for CNABU's
manipulation_enhanced_map_prediction and view-point-pushing did not include a
license granting code reuse. This repository therefore uses only a clean-room
implementation of mathematical and interface ideas described in the published
papers; none of those repositories' code or assets has been copied.

Optional dependency
-------------------

pomdp_py is offered only as an optional, separately installed dependency. It
is distributed by its authors under the MIT License:
https://github.com/h2r/pomdp-py/blob/main/LICENSE

Software and model licenses are separate. In particular, OpenVLA source code
is MIT-licensed while released model weights may inherit restrictions from
their base models. Users are responsible for reviewing the licenses of all
optional code, weights, datasets, robot assets and simulator resources they
connect to this project.
